# Responsive & mobile shell

Perovo ships as **Capacitor APK**, **Play Store TWA**, and **iOS Capacitor**. One codebase; **bottom nav only** (no desktop top bar).

## Localhost dev

- `src/ui/dev/DevPhoneFrame.jsx` wraps the app on `localhost` — full-screen phone frame with device size picker
- `html[data-dev-phone-frame="1"]` forces mobile shell CSS even on wide laptop viewports
- Helpers: `src/utils/devPhoneFrame.js`

## Viewport & safe area

- `index.html` keeps `viewport-fit=cover` and boot styles using `100dvh`
- Page padding uses `env(safe-area-inset-*)` via `.ct-main` — do not stack extra `16px` margins on page sections
- Bottom nav, FAB, and sticky CTAs account for `safe-area-inset-bottom`

## Layout rules

- **No fixed page widths** ≥300px without `max-width` or a `@media` breakpoint
- Prefer `ct-stack`, `ct-row-between`, `ct-grid-2` over ad-hoc flex with pixel widths
- Use `min-w-0` on flex children that contain truncating text
- Avoid `100vw` on full-width elements — use `100%` or `ct-page` instead
- Prefer `dvh` over `vh` for full-screen panels and auth gates

## Components

- `PageShell` for top-level pages
- Bottom sheets (`Modal sheet`) max-height uses `dvh` + safe-area
- Segmented controls and chip rows wrap or scroll — never clip on 320px screens

## Governance

```bash
npm run audit:mobile
npm run audit:native-shells
npm run roger:all
```
